# Agile Sprint Plan (Week 01 to Week 09)

## Project Title

**Development of NegoSphere: AI-Driven Multi-Agent Negotiation Training & Simulation Platform**

---

## Sprint Overview Summary

NegoSphere is developed in iterative stages covering project architecture, scenario management, multi-agent negotiation logic, Simulation Mode, Practice Mode, learning insights, reporting, platform integration, and release validation.

The sprint plan below adapts the nine-week structure to NegoSphere. Sprint story-point values, completion percentages, and defect counts are intentionally not fabricated; use the team's accepted backlog and sprint records to populate those metrics.

| Sprint | Week | Primary Theme | Planned Deliverables | Key Validation |
|:---:|:---:|---|---|---|
| Sprint 1 | Week 1 (Days 01–05) | Requirements, Architecture & Setup | Review existing architecture, document services and configuration, establish sprint backlog and acceptance criteria. | Confirm local setup and service boundaries. |
| Sprint 2 | Week 2 (Days 06–10) | Scenario Library & Custom Scenario Setup | Review predefined scenarios, scenario search/navigation, custom scenario form and agent configuration. | Validate scenario selection and configuration flow. |
| Sprint 3 | Week 3 (Days 11–15) | Negotiation Engine & Orchestration | Validate turn-taking, offers, counteroffers, constraints, concessions, acceptance, rejection, and deadlock. | Run core negotiation verification. |
| Sprint 4 | Week 4 (Days 16–20) | Simulation Mode | Verify AI-versus-AI round progression, transcript updates, stance indicators, and terminal outcomes. | Confirm results are revealed in the correct sequence. |
| Sprint 5 | Week 5 (Days 21–25) | Practice Mode & Realistic Decisions | Verify user offer submission, AI response decisions, offer boundaries, and realistic negotiation behavior. | Test acceptance, counteroffer, rejection, and deadlock cases. |
| Sprint 6 | Week 6 (Days 26–30) | Learning Experience | Review tactic explanations, turning points, key takeaways, and observed negotiation skills. | Ensure explanations are grounded in session history. |
| Sprint 7 | Week 7 (Days 31–35) | Reports, Analytics & Session History | Validate KPIs, transcript, final terms, exports, completed-session history, and outcome integrity. | Compare report values with the actual session state. |
| Sprint 8 | Week 8 (Days 36–40) | Dashboard, Profile & Platform Integration | Review dashboard metrics, recent activity, profile/settings, frontend/backend communication, and persistence. | Run relevant integration and dashboard checks. |
| Sprint 9 | Week 9 (Days 41–45) | Regression, Documentation & Release Readiness | Run relevant verification scripts, review build/lint status, update README and Agile documents, record known limitations. | Record actual results for each release check. |

